Finished in a dark metallic brown, silver, and gold scheme, "Tank" was engineered to withstand severe physical punishment while providing heavy suppressive fire. Tony designed its armor panels to absorb high-impact kinetic force, making it ideal for clearing heavily fortified enemy lines or holding down a defensive choke point single-handedly.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XXIV answers the call during the House Party Protocol at the Norco oil rig, engaging Extremis soldiers in heavy ground combat alongside the rest of the Iron Legion before being destroyed in the final "Clean Slate" detonation order.
